# lexicon .env.example — variable names tracked; real values live in .env (gitignored)

# --- OpenSubtitles API + consumer (for subtitle-verification of TV/film cards) ---
# Sign up at https://www.opensubtitles.com/en/users/sign_up then create a consumer at
# https://www.opensubtitles.com/en/consumers — free tier ~5 downloads/day, ~100 searches/day;
# VIP tier substantially higher. All four vars are OPTIONAL — workflows that need subtitles
# skip gracefully if unset.
#
# Sibling-share note: github.com/justinstimatze/cupel already holds VIP-tier
# credentials for this same account; lexicon's .env is a copy lifted from there.
OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY=
# OPENSUBTITLES_USER_AGENT must match the consumer name + version you registered.
OPENSUBTITLES_USER_AGENT=
OPENSUBTITLES_USERNAME=
OPENSUBTITLES_PASSWORD=
